  "comments": "In the post-war years, mainly 1948 and 1950, 5 and 10 Reichspfennig (Third German Reich, KM #100 / #101) that were still remaining in Austria were struck over due to a lack of round material. The overstamped pfennig coin (KM#97) is very rare with details of the original coin often remaining visible.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a38c2e57df19.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5a38c2e57df19.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a38c2f970626.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5a38c2f970626.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThose coins frequently show bubbles, a defect of zinc coins:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5cf8cb8b3ffca.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5cf8cb8b3ffca.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a>",
